    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "AIDL versions are frozen as API snapshots built with aidl_interface.",
      "narration": "An aidl_interface module in Android.bp declares the interface. Freezing it saves a snapshot under aidl_api, and later versions may only append compatibly.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Versioning",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "aidl_interface {\n    name: \"android.hardware.foo\",\n    srcs: [\"IFoo.aidl\"],\n    stability: \"vintf\",\n    backend: {\n        ndk: { enabled: true },\n    },\n}",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 30,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "hl",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "c",
          "at": 4000,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Frozen versions live in aidl_api/",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 54,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "gray",
          "at": 5500,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "AIDL offers Java, C++, NDK and Rust backends; HIDL's tooling was a dead end.",
      "narration": "With AIDL, one interface gets Java, NDK and Rust bindings, and there is only one IPC stack to maintain. HIDL stopped receiving new features.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Why migrate",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "l",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "one IPC stack, one toolchain",
            "NDK and Rust backends",
            "stable ABI, frozen versions",
            "HIDL: no new features"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 32,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 7000,
      "caption": "New HALs should be AIDL; HIDL is kept for old releases.",
      "narration": "In practice that means new HALs use stable AIDL, and HIDL survives only for older interfaces.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
